WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:12.220
Calm on the Nifty, fireworks underneath. Good evening, and welcome to Closing Bell on the Nivesh Desk.

2
00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:16.700
Here are tonight's headlines.

3
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:22.160
The Nifty ends flat on expiry day, but smallcaps sprint more than two percent.

4
00:00:22.610 --> 00:00:28.320
Foreign investors turn buyers, with their biggest day of buying since early September.

5
00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:35.060
Results-day rallies in OneSource, Sona BLW, Mankind Pharma and Tata Consumer.

6
00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:40.770
And cement cracks. All of it, straight from the Smart Trading Desk.

7
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:54.950
First, the scoreboard. The Nifty 50 settled at 22,749.75, down just three and a half points, as the October series expired.

8
00:00:55.400 --> 00:01:09.250
Bank Nifty dragged, down 0.7 percent. But beneath the surface, the Smallcap 250 jumped 2.2 percent, the Next 50 rose 1.3, and the Midcap 150 gained 0.9.

9
00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:20.240
Breadth was strong. About two and a half stocks rose for every one that fell, and India VIX cooled 4.4 percent, to 16.4.

10
00:01:20.690 --> 00:01:26.620
Still, the desk's market regime reads Bear, so its new-trade size limits stay halved.

11
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:38.050
To earnings. The desk's Results Week tracker shows 103 companies have declared so far, with 382 still to come.

12
00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:48.530
With no analyst consensus in the system, the desk scores each quarter against the company's own trend: 4 above, 31 in line, 5 below.

13
00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:57.930
OneSource Specialty Pharma rocketed 13.8 percent on 36 times its usual volume, after its profit grew more than five-fold.

14
00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:11.800
Sona BLW gained 9 percent, Eris 8.4, and Mankind Pharma 8.2. In the Nifty 50, Tata Consumer rose 6.8 percent on five times normal volume.

15
00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:25.330
On the downside, Aequs fell 9.6 percent, and Dalmia Bharat 6.6, on ten times its usual volume. REC slipped 3.9 percent after a 21 percent drop in profit.

16
00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:41.120
After the bell, the heavyweights reported. Bajaj Auto's profit rose 62 percent, to 3,436 crore rupees. L and T's rose 32.5 percent, and Radico's jumped 66.

17
00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:51.640
But Maruti's profit fell 26 percent, Cipla's 35, Mazagon Dock's 54, and ACC's 92. They all react tomorrow.

18
00:02:54.000 --> 00:03:05.140
Sector rotation now. Media led the indices, up 3.7 percent, with Capital Goods, Realty, Pharma, Telecom and Power all up around 2 percent.

19
00:03:05.590 --> 00:03:15.840
Financials lagged, with the bank indices down 0.7 percent. Cement was the weakest, down 2 percent, with 10 of its 12 stocks in the red.

20
00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:30.730
Over a month, IT leads, up 14 percent, while Metals and Consumer Durables are down more than 9 percent each. The desk's rotation matrix tags IT, Telecom and Consumer Services as leading.

21
00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:46.080
Movers and shakers, index by index. The Nifty 50 split 25 to 25. Tata Consumer and Bharti Airtel led, while Asian Paints, Coal India and Grasim fell the most.

22
00:03:46.530 --> 00:04:00.930
In the Nifty 100, advancers won 61 to 39. Hitachi Energy jumped 5.8 percent and Divi's 5, while Mazagon Dock sank 6.5 percent on six times its usual volume.

23
00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:12.950
The Nifty 200 went 128 to 72. Mankind topped the board at 8.2 percent, and M and M Financial was the worst, down 6.6.

24
00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:27.990
And in the Nifty 500, 356 stocks rose. Ola Electric surged 16.2 percent, OneSource 13.8 and Sun TV 10.9, while Aegis Logistics fell 7 percent.

25
00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:39.190
By sector: every media and realty stock in the 500 rose, and 18 of 19 power names. Construction materials managed just one gainer in eleven.

26
00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:56.450
Follow the money. Provisional data show FIIs bought a net 4,240 crore rupees in cash today, their biggest buying day since the second of September. DIIs sold 1,250 crore.

27
00:04:56.900 --> 00:05:14.230
A rare role reversal. For October, FIIs are still net sellers of about 48,700 crore, and DIIs net buyers of 60,500 crore. Over three months, FIIs sold over one lakh crore, while DIIs bought over two lakh crore.

28
00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:23.700
The desk's flow chart runs to Monday; today's figures join with the next load. One day of buying is a signal, not yet a trend.

29
00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:36.630
Now, the desk's Top 10 ideas. These are ideas for review, not recommendations, and the desk's own scorecard shows no measurable ranking skill yet.

30
00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:50.330
ICICI Bank and Coforge lead the cash list. Coforge closed just 0.6 percent below resistance at 2,008.80, on 1.6 times average volume.

31
00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:59.950
Sagility, Anand Rathi, Union Bank, GE Shipping, Persistent, Mankind, Sona BLW and Petronet complete the ten.

32
00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:21.020
The F and O board reads a mixed regime with a falling trend, so it fits defined-risk bear put spreads, like the Nifty 22,350 to 22,750 spread for 3 November. The desk flags that this conflicts with the bullish cash setups, so those rows are information only.

33
00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:31.290
Tomorrow: India's industrial production data at 4 PM, and the US Fed decision at 11:30 PM India time.

34
00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:40.910
Plus reactions to Bajaj Auto, Maruti, L and T and Cipla, and results from Hindustan Unilever, Adani Enterprises and Vedanta.

35
00:06:41.360 --> 00:06:44.340
That's Closing Bell from the Nivesh Desk.

36
00:06:44.780 --> 00:06:50.920
Market information and education, not investment advice. Good night.
